      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-252131",
      ":question/problem": "Suppose $X_{1}, X_{2}, \u2026, X_{8}$ is an I.I.D. random sample with $X_{i}\u223cExp(\u03b8)$, where $\u03b8$ is an unknown parameter. For a particular sample $x_{1}, x_{2}, \u2026, x_{8}$, you're given that\n$\u2211_(i = 1)^(8)x_{i}^{2} = 4$.\n\nFind the method of moments estimate $\u03b8^(^)_{MM}$ for $\u03b8$."
